//
// Each piece's duration is its own arc length divided by that speed, so the boundaries
// fall out of the geometry. Consecutive pieces share their end face -- the legs share the
// A's apex face, the right leg and the trail share the foot cut, the trail and the
// crossbar share the hoop's left hook face -- so the speed is continuous across every
// join with nothing tuned: the face's own length is the width both sides agree on.
//
// Seconds from the start of play. The easings are linear() timing functions carrying the
// speed law itself, so a piece's progress is never linear in its own window.

